1
00:00:02,220 --> 00:00:03,880
Alice ran away?!

2
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:05,290
Yeah.

3
00:00:05,373 --> 00:00:06,957
I think she might have
been overwhelmed by all

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,357
the interviews and things
we had scheduled for her.

5
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:12,657
I always checked with her to see if
she was tired and needed a break,

6
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:16,328
but she'd just smile and shake
her head and say she was fine.

7
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,657
I'll head to the Roppongi
office right now.

8
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:26,505
Once we find out where she's at,
we can all go get her together.

9
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:35,420
Now what?

10
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:41,590
Alice!

11
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:48,340
You need to sign for it.

12
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:54,120
It's from Wrath.

13
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,140
I wonder what they sent me.

14
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:21,240
Would you stop making so much
noise and kindly unpack me?

15
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:22,900
Now, please.

16
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:35,280
Jeez, Alice.

17
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,580
Everyone's worried sick about you.

18
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:38,770
I know.

19
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:40,540
I am sorry about that.

20
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:41,995
It was very childish.

21
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:44,993
I was desperate to speak with you alone.

22
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:48,820
And not in your virtual form,
but your real physical self.

23
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:51,460
Just you and I, face to face.

24
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:53,610
Kirito.

25
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:56,080
I am so angry with you.

26
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:58,857
Why did you not tell me
you were staying behind?

27
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:01,980
and of the possibility
you would never return.

28
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:06,597
If you had told me before I
reached the altar, I would have...

29
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,077
I would have...

30
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:11,140
I would have stayed and not fled here!

31
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:14,580
I am still a knight.

32
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:16,740
Fighting evil is my duty.

33
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,317
So why...

34
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,200
Why did you face him alone?

35
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:23,077
A dreadful foe like that,
what were you thinking?

36
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:26,631
Why did you not want me there,
by your side, assisting you?

37
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:34,700
Who do you think I, Alice
Synthesis 30, am, if not capable?

38
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:37,440
Who am I in your eyes?

39
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:44,760
That's easy.

40
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:46,340
You're my hope.

41
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:50,100
And you're not just my hope.

42
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:51,555
The Underworlds, too.

43
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:54,057
All the people who lived and died there.

44
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:55,905
A hope that can't be replaced.

45
00:02:56,940 --> 00:02:58,520
I didn't want to lose you.

46
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:02,646
I wanted to protect you so that
hope could last for the future.

47
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:08,510
Really?

48
00:03:08,593 --> 00:03:11,500
This future, what do you
think it will look like?

49
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:16,120
If I can endure the loneliness
and chaos of this world,

50
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,457
trapped inside this body made of steel,

51
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:21,540
what kind of future could
there possibly be for me?

52
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:24,290
Sorry.

53
00:03:24,373 --> 00:03:27,500
I wish I had an answer for that, but...

54
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:32,942
I know that you being here
will change the world,

55
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:35,338
and you'll change it for the better.

56
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:39,465
And when all's said and
done, Cardinal's hopes,

57
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:41,037
and Administrators,

58
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:47,820
and Bercouli's, and Eldrie's, and Eugeo's
too, will finally become a reality.

59
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:49,554
That's what I believe.

60
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:58,200
We must contact Rank at once.

61
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:02,060
It simply will not do to
make her worry further.

62
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:05,140
Mm-hmm. Good idea.

63
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,070
Hey.

64
00:04:12,153 --> 00:04:15,217
Yeah, she's here. She's
fine. Uh-huh. Sure.

65
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,220
Okay, bye.

66
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,440
She says hi.

67
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:22,557
Don't worry, she's not upset.

68
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:25,816
She feels bad, you know, for
all you're going through.

69
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:30,331
She also said you can spend
the night here, if you want it.

70
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:33,820
She said I could? Really? Yep.

71
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:38,262
If that is the case, I would like
you to show me around your home.

72
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:40,960
You will, won't you?

73
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:45,117
I have never seen the inside of a
real-world dwelling space before.

74
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:47,277
Sure, no problem.

75
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:50,380
But like, it's not really that special.

76
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,798
There's not a whole lot more to see.

77
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:57,380
Actually, you'll like this part of it.

78
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:10,410
Amazing.

79
00:05:10,493 --> 00:05:11,837
Is this a training hall?

80
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:12,820
Uh-huh.

81
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:15,436
But in this world, we call it a dojo.

82
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,060
A dojo.

83
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:27,530
Interesting.

84
00:05:27,613 --> 00:05:29,497
Such a peculiar training sword.

85
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,227
Quite different from
those in the Underworld.

86
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:38,650
Oh?

87
00:05:38,733 --> 00:05:39,620
What's up?

88
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:40,970
Take it.

89
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,680
This is a training hall.

90
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:45,340
Let us make use of it.

91
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:46,980
Wait, what?

92
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:49,980
I don't know about this.

93
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:51,960
Are you used to that body?

94
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:54,920
No need to hold back.

95
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:04,940
Do you remember?

96
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:08,237
The day you and I first crossed swords in

97
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:10,377
the garden on the 80th
floor of the cathedral.

98
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:13,377
Yeah, you clobbered the
hell out of me back there.

99
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:15,578
I'm not gonna let that happen again.

100
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:53,880
I win again.

101
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:57,340
Thanks to my ultimate
skill, the steel headbutt.

102
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:01,060
I never heard of that one before.

103
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:02,438
I just invented it.

104
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:09,060
I will be alright now, Kirito.

105
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:12,477
I know I can survive in this world.

106
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:17,320
Wherever I go, I will be myself
as long as I can wield a sword.

107
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:24,260
I have realized that my fight is
not over yet, and neither is yours.

108
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:31,200
So I will look forward, and only
forward, and keep moving ahead.

109
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:36,140
Then Kazuto tripped and fell. Really?

110
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:38,437
It is hard to believe he was so clumsy.

111
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:39,900
Oh, he was.

112
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:41,611
I could tell you stories.

113
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:45,440
Kazuto, we have a lot to talk about.

114
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:50,780
First things first, I believe you owe
your mother and I a proper apology.

115
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:03,640
Father, Mother, I didn't
mean to make you guys worry.

116
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:05,160
I'm really sorry.

117
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,700
We're used to it by now.

118
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:12,917
Besides, this time, what you were doing
was something very important, right?

119
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,765
If you say you're going
to do something, do it.

120
00:08:16,060 --> 00:08:19,177
It's the same with writing a
book or sticking to a deadline.

121
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:21,200
Oh, Mom, that's your experience.

122
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,864
Your mother left something out.

123
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:29,045
For days, she had no idea where you were,
and she was getting sick from worrying.

124
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:32,117
I understand the importance
of what you accomplished.

125
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,729
However, that does not
mean you get a pass.

126
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:37,660
Kazuto, where should your focus be now?

127
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:41,140
On high school. That's it. Exactly.

128
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:44,157
And that's where you should be
putting all of your efforts,

129
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:47,760
not just during class,
but all the time. I know.

130
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:50,077
I have to study hard and get into college.

131
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:52,677
It's already the summer
of your junior year.

132
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:56,380
Your mother said you wanted to
go to America and study there.

133
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:57,972
Is that still your plan?

134
00:08:58,460 --> 00:09:01,520
Well, I was thinking about that and...

135
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:04,060
I'm sorry.

136
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,340
I sort of changed my mind.

137
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:07,860
Sort of how?

138
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:11,177
I still want to major in
electrical engineering,

139
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:13,860
but here, at Toto Institute, actually.

140
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,597
After that, I want to work at, or,

141
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:21,600
I mean, the Oceanic Exploration
and Research Institute.

142
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,317
Father, excuse me?

143
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:37,060
When I first presented myself
as a knight to my father,

144
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:39,340
I am sure he had his reservations.

145
00:09:39,940 --> 00:09:43,657
Through my actions, I proved to
him the depth of my conviction.

146
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:47,799
And I am sure in the end, he understood
my choice to remain a knight.

147
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:53,460
Kirito, or rather Kazuto, also
follows the path he believes is just.

148
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:58,400
And I know this, because despite being
an ordinary student in this world,

149
00:09:58,620 --> 00:10:01,720
in my world, he was the
greatest swordsman of all.

150
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:05,397
One who fought gallantly to
protect countless others.

151
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:06,340
He is a hero.

152
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:07,930
Alice.

153
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:09,940
Yes, I know.

154
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,377
In fact, his mother and I know
about everything he's done.

155
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:17,860
He's as much of a hero in
this world as he was in yours.

156
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,320
Aren't you, Black Swordsman?

157
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:22,650
Kazuto.

158
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:28,117
To choose a path, to study, to
attend a university and get a job.

159
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:32,340
Those are just part of a process
and the fruits of your labor,

160
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:34,397
but it's okay to change your mind.

161
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:36,277
Just try to live without regrets.

162
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:38,007
That's all we expect of you.

163
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:45,620
I will, promise.

164
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:48,210
Thanks, Dad.

165
00:10:48,293 --> 00:10:49,123
Thanks, Mom.

166
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:05,700
Kirito, wake up.

167
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:07,450
Kirito.

168
00:11:13,700 --> 00:11:14,530
Huh?

169
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:19,320
Alice! Shh!

170
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:21,348
Would you lower your voice?

171
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,757
Yeah, sorry, it's just that...

172
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:25,320
What are you doing here?

173
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:27,840
Wearing next to nothing.

174
00:11:29,860 --> 00:11:30,690
I...

175
00:11:30,773 --> 00:11:32,180
I demand you stop leering!

176
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:37,570
Alright.

177
00:11:37,653 --> 00:11:39,220
It's late. What's up?

178
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:44,297
Approximately five minutes ago, while I
was connected to your so-called network,

179
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:49,027
I received an alarming communique via
your world's remote messaging formal art.

180
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:51,180
Email? Who's it from?

181
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:53,517
It had no name ascribed to it.

182
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:55,537
They wrote...

183
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:58,267
Actually, it would be
quicker if you read it.

184
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:10,260
What the hell?

185
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:21,120
Yui, are you up?

186
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:24,860
I am now, Daddy. Good morning.

187
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:26,617
Sorry to wake you.

188
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:28,340
I need a favor. Sure.

189
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:29,740
Check this out.

190
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:34,190
Interesting.

191
00:12:34,273 --> 00:12:37,195
These are the names of floors
in the Central Cathedral.

192
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:39,710
Yes.

193
00:12:39,793 --> 00:12:41,180
Training Hall 2 is Floor 52.

194
00:12:41,620 --> 00:12:43,560
Media Storage is Floor 68.

195
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:45,257
The Senate is on 96.

196
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:47,380
Geographical Records is Floor 58.

197
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:52,920
Look at that.

198
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:55,540
An IP address. Yes.

199
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:59,777
It seems the white
tower to climb is the IP

200
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:02,217
address you deciphered
from the second line.

201
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:05,797
If that's so, you're supposed
to follow it to reach Yon World.

202
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:10,060
So basically, it says this
address is pointing to a server.

203
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:13,040
Yeah, that's it. I get it now.

204
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,300
Here it is.

205
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:16,872
It's the way back there.

206
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:20,460
This is the path leading
to the Underworld!

207
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:23,340
The way back? Really?

208
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:26,097
Then that means we can...

209
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:29,480
I can return to my world.

210
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:32,360
My home. My people.

211
00:13:33,660 --> 00:13:34,490
Yeah.

212
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:46,873
Now that that's settled, I was thinking
when we go back to the Underworld,

213
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:51,080
Um, is it cool if Asuna comes along too?

214
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:55,720
I suppose so.

215
00:13:56,280 --> 00:13:58,140
If we find ourselves in danger,

216
00:13:58,260 --> 00:14:01,672
we'll need as many warriors
at our disposal as we can get.

217
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:06,340
Here it is.

218
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:11,730
Funny.

219
00:14:11,813 --> 00:14:14,100
I get the feeling he might be behind this.

220
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:15,450
Me too.

221
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:16,840
He probably is.

222
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:25,435
Yui, did you find anything
else out about that address?

223
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:28,819
I could only get as far as
the server's relay point.

224
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:33,600
The firewall it has is super tough, so
I couldn't go any further. It's okay.

225
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:34,770
You tried.

226
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:36,940
Well, it's time we dove in.

227
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:39,005
We shouldn't be in any danger.

228
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,460
I think.

229
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:43,701
If you get in trouble,
I'll swoop in and save you!

230
00:14:44,100 --> 00:14:45,276
Damn right you will.

231
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:46,900
Okay, see ya.

232
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:52,200
Remember, a couple
hundred years have passed.

233
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:56,097
The Human Empire and Dark Territory
could be way different now.

234
00:14:56,180 --> 00:14:58,062
Watch your backs in there, okay?

235
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:02,260
Okay, but Administrator ruled
the Human Empire for 300 years.

236
00:15:02,580 --> 00:15:04,817
That's a bit longer than we've been gone.

237
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:07,040
I doubt it's changed all that much.

238
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:12,420
When we log in, the first thing
we'll do is go wake Selka up.

239
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:13,870
Mm-hmm.

240
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:18,140
Thank you, Kirito. Asuna.

241
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,340
All right, guys.

242
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:24,180
Are you ready to dive in? Ready!

243
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:45,100
What's this?

244
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:50,840
We were in outer space!

245
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:58,000
Kirito, look there.

246
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,680
No way!

247
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:38,790
Underworld!

248
00:16:38,873 --> 00:16:39,720
Land of my birth!

249
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:42,117
Land where I was nurtured and raised!

250
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,140
Hear me now!

251
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:46,200
At last, I have returned to you.

252
00:16:48,860 --> 00:16:50,340
Your daughter...

253
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:52,400
HAS RETURNED!

254
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:12,760
Laura! You okay? Come in!

255
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:15,320
Hasty, I'm here.

256
00:17:15,580 --> 00:17:18,940
I'm okay for now, but my ship's not.

257
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:21,000
She's on her last leg.

258
00:17:21,780 --> 00:17:22,637
That's it, then.

259
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:23,779
You have to eject.

260
00:17:24,060 --> 00:17:27,377
The thrusters on your flight suit
should get you back to Garden.

261
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:28,290
No way!

262
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:30,880
That's not happening.

263
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:32,860
I can't just abandon her!

264
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:35,840
You're right. You can't.

265
00:17:40,340 --> 00:17:42,077
We're gonna fight to the end, then.

266
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:43,020
You and me.

267
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:46,100
Roger that.

268
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:08,337
It's a...

269
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,580
a man!

270
00:18:25,220 --> 00:18:27,985
He can't fight that thing
with a couple swords.

271
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:33,675
Release recollection.

272
00:18:52,180 --> 00:18:54,460
Release Recollection!

273
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:33,280
Did they kill it?

274
00:19:34,520 --> 00:19:36,040
I think they killed it.

275
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:38,100
That monster's not dead yet.

276
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:42,990
Watch out!

277
00:19:43,073 --> 00:19:43,939
It's getting away!

278
00:19:44,060 --> 00:19:46,648
We have to burn it up
before it regenerates!

279
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:57,137
That Swordsman...

280
00:19:57,220 --> 00:19:58,837
That knight...

281
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:00,300
I've seen her before.

282
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:02,500
Yeah, so have I.

283
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:04,320
It's Lady Alice.

284
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:09,880
Release recollection.

285
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,880
She did it.

286
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:44,560
Oh my gosh!

287
00:20:45,020 --> 00:20:45,960
Do you look it?

288
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:47,062
Do you see him?

289
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:49,520
The man wearing black! I know him!

290
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:51,390
Yeah, Laura.

291
00:20:51,473 --> 00:20:52,303
I do too.

292
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:53,500
I do too.

293
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:14,700
What color of your soul
is the color of your soul?

294
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,270
I don't know.

295
00:21:54,060 --> 00:21:56,760
Thank you.

296
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:57,740
Thank you.

297
00:23:24,420 --> 00:23:25,250
Thank you.
